cluttered to being in a hoarding home, right? Exactly right. And really what we say in the APA, DSM, the diagnostic and statistical manual of disorders, is that it has to cause distress, but it's more likely that, in my experience, that hoarding causes impairment. So we say distress or impairment. People who hoard, usually hoard things that don't have a lot of value to most people. They buy in bulk. They acquire so many things that people can't move through their homes. It can cause a fire hazard, a safety hazard. In extreme cases, people will lose their homes or they will lose their children. So it can really become very dire for people. Absolutely. And why do people with hoarding disorder have such a hard time letting things go? As you mentioned, a lot of times it's things that

