people because there's certainly progress to be made. And I have had people contact me years later to say, hey, I just moved cross-country and it was fine. So it's really exciting to hear that kind of thing. And I also think it's important to be realistic that this is a very complex problem that didn't develop overnight. It is genetically loaded. These are behaviors that have been entrenched for a long time. There are often, as we mentioned, other moving parts, meaning the person may suffer from other anxiety problems or ADHD. In terms of medication, there is currently no medication that is considered particularly effective for hoarding disorder. That is not to say that medications can't be helpful, though, because like we've talked about, there are often other problems going on. So if a person

